        "content" : "Proof. Suppose that k ≥ 4. Let G′ = (G−xx1)+x1x4. Note that x1x2x3x4v1 is a pendent 4-cycle at x4 in G′. Note that |V (G′)| = n, |E(G′)| = |E(G)|, and G′ has more pendent 4-cycles than G."
