    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Suppose that degG(x) = 2. Let H be the connected component containing xk. Then |V (H)| ≤ n − 6. If H ̸= C8, then for a minimum hop dominating set S of H, we have |S| ≤ 2(n−56)+2 by (3.1), and so S ∪ {v,x} is a hop dominating set of G whose size is at most 25n, a contradiction. Thus H = C8. Then G is one of the last two graphs in Figure 6, which shows that γh(G) ≤ 25n. This completes the proof of our main theorem."
